==Finnish==

===Etymology===
{{etyl|ru|fi}} {{term|гласность||openness|tr=glasnost|sc=Cyrl}}
The root of the word "glasnost" is "glas" or "глас", which is an Old Russian word for "voice". Thus, "glasnost" means "open voice" implying transparency and revelation of any issue to the public by the government (at least, it was the intent of the concept).

